+   "source": [
+    "### Optuna study — LGBM refinement\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Refines the LGBM hyperparameters around the optimum found in commit `e4e8d5d`\n",
+    "(broad 50-trial search via `src.tuning.lgbm_objective`). Worth re-running since\n",
+    "the data has changed: `TotalDiscount` was added to `fe_v1` after that study ran.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Differences from the broad space in `src/tuning.py` — ranges are centred on the\n",
+    "previous best, plus three deliberate changes:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "- **`num_leaves` capped at 64** — with `max_depth ≤ 6` a tree has at most 2⁶\n",
+    "  leaves, so larger values are dead knobs (the old best's `num_leaves=249`\n",
+    "  never bound at `max_depth=4`).\n",
+    "- **`min_split_gain` and `n_estimators` upper bounds raised** — the old best\n",
+    "  sat near the previous caps (0.886 of 1.0, 874 of 1000).\n",
+    "- **`learning_rate` floor raised to 0.05** — small-lr trials can't converge\n",
+    "  within the tree budget and waste trials.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Trial 0 is the e4e8d5d optimum itself (`enqueue_trial`), so the study starts at\n",
+    "the known best on the inner-CV metric. Budget: 50 trials × 3-fold CV on 594k\n",
+    "rows — expect roughly 15–25 min on CPU. **Skippable**: the run config below\n",
+    "falls back to the stored e4e8d5d params when this cell hasn't been run."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 41,
